    {
      "id": "beab7ddd-37a7-4d60-9b23-d47cce046b0c",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -640,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## 08-19-01 automate fitness studio class attendance and member retention with AI\n\n### How it works\n\nThe front desk records every class check-in on a webhook. The member is matched against the MemberRoster sheet and an AI agent judges whether they are at risk, new or engaged and writes a short personal message. Every check-in is logged to the AttendanceLog sheet and the member gets their message by email. No-shows and at-risk members also alert the manager on Discord. Every Monday a weekly report with attendance stats, at-risk members, new members and an AI summary is emailed to the manager and posted on Discord.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Create a Google Sheet with two tabs, MemberRoster and AttendanceLog, using the exact column headers from the workflow nodes.\n- Fill the MemberRoster tab with every member id, name, email, membership, join date and a yes or no email flag.\n- Connect Google Sheets, Gmail, OpenAI and Discord credentials on the matching nodes.\n- Point your front desk app at the fitness/checkin webhook.\n- Set the weekly report schedule and the manager email address.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the AI prompts, add your own class names, or swap Discord for Telegram or Slack."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
